  "verbalization": "Prednisone appears to be linked to Richter Syndrome through a series of indirect pathways involving leukemia and immunomodulatory treatments. The evidence suggests that Prednisone is associated with Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia, which in turn is linked to drugs like Ofatumumab and Duvelisib. These drugs are known to be used in the treatment of leukemia, and their association with Richter Syndrome implies a potential role in the progression of the disease. The indirect connection through these medications highlights a possible mechanism where Prednisone may influence the course of leukemia, potentially contributing to the development of Richter Syndrome. The evidence is supported by a combination of indication links and the presence of a shared target in the pathophysiology of the disease, though the exact mechanism remains unclear.",
